# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# Gerber: 4♣ asks for aces over partner's natural notrump, where no suit
# has been agreed. Answers by steps (4♦ 0 or 4, 4♥ 1, 4♠ 2, 4NT 3); 5♣
# then asks for kings the same way. The asker places the contract; 4NT
# after an answer is a sign-off. Notes: gerber.notes.md.
#
# Where it applies (card `slam.gerber.*`):
# - directly over partner's 1NT or 2NT opening, and over 2♣–2♦–2NT;
# - over partner's 1NT or 2NT rebid after 1x–1y, unless the card says
#   `gerber.only_over_nt_openings` (BBA's "Gerber only for NT openings").
# Never where clubs are natural or a suit is agreed: after a transfer, a
# Stayman answer, or a minor raise, 4♣ keeps its other meanings.
#
# 4♣ over 1NT is a transfer to diamonds with `transfers.texas_4c`, and
# then Gerber is off there. Over 2NT the 4♣ slam try in clubs
# (two-nt-responses.bid) is off when Gerber is on: those hands ask for
# aces and bid 6♣ (gerber.notes.md, "Decisions").

module gerber "Gerber: 4♣ asks for aces over partner's notrump"
  card   slam.gerber.play
  needs  notrump-base
  param  only_openings = slam.gerber.only_over_nt_openings default false
  param  texas_4c = notrump.transfers.texas_4c default false
  param  style = general.style

# ── The ask ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The hands that would bid 6NT directly (one-nt.bid, two-nt-responses.bid)
# check the aces first; priority 1 puts the ask ahead of 6NT. BBA asks a
# point lower, 31 HCP between the hands (probes/gerber-resp-1N.toml,
# gerber-resp-2N.toml), and then bids 6NT only with three aces between
# the hands: that is the bba treatment. Our default keeps Rick's 4NT
# invitation with 16 opposite 15-17 (one-nt.bid).
after 1N (P) when !texas_4c
  4C  "Gerber: how many aces?"  alert
      shows balanced, points>=32-partner.hcp.min, H<=4, S<=4   # a major goes through Stayman or a transfer
      when  style is not bba
      sets  ask=gerber
      artificial
      priority 1                         # ahead of 6NT: check the aces first
  4C  "Gerber: how many aces?"  alert
      shows balanced, hcp>=31-partner.hcp.min, H<=4, S<=4
      when  style is bba
      sets  ask=gerber
      artificial
      priority 1

# Over 2NT a long club suit asks too, and plays in 6♣ (BBA from 9 HCP
# with six clubs; our threshold is the old 4♣ slam try's).
after 2N (P) | 2C (P) 2D (P) 2N (P)
  4C  "Gerber: how many aces?"  alert
      shows H<=4, S<=4, (balanced, strength>=slam) | (C>=6 | (C>=5, !balanced), strength>=slam_invite)
      when  style is not bba
      sets  ask=gerber
      artificial
      priority 1
  4C  "Gerber: how many aces?"  alert
      shows H<=4, S<=4, (balanced, hcp>=31-partner.hcp.min) | (C>=6, hcp>=29-partner.hcp.min)
      when  style is bba
      sets  ask=gerber
      artificial
      priority 1

after 1x (P) 1y (P) 1N (P) | 1x (P) 1y (P) 2N (P) when !only_openings
  4C  "Gerber: how many aces?"  alert
      shows balanced, points>=32-partner.hcp.min
      sets  ask=gerber
      artificial
      priority 1

# ── The answers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
when asked gerber
  4D  "0 or 4 aces"   shows keycards(N) in 0|4   artificial
  4H  "1 ace"         shows keycards(N)=1        artificial
  4S  "2 aces"        shows keycards(N)=2        artificial
  4N  "3 aces"        shows keycards(N)=3        artificial

# ── The asker places the contract ─────────────────────────────────────
# we.keycards(N) is my aces plus partner's answer, four in the deck, so
# "0 or 4" resolves against my own. Rules without `shows` rank by
# priority, then file order: the grand before the king ask before six.
# The thresholds (my points plus opener's minimum) were set on the
# corpus: 7NT from 35 with all the aces, the king ask at 33-34
# (gerber.notes.md, "Grand slam and the king ask"; the textbook 37 for
# 7NT scored 400 IMPs worse).
when answered gerber
  7N  "Grand slam: all the aces and 35 between us"
      when  we.keycards(N)=4, points + partner.hcp.min >= 35
      priority 3
  5C  "Gerber: how many kings?"  alert
      when  we.keycards(N)=4, points + partner.hcp.min >= 33, points + partner.hcp.min <= 34
      when  C<=5                         # a long club suit settles for six
      sets  ask=gerber_kings
      artificial
      priority 2
  6C  "Slam in clubs: at most one ace missing"
      when  we.keycards(N)>=3, C>=6, imps       # at matchpoints 6NT scored better (notes)
      priority 1
  6N  "Small slam: at most one ace missing"
      when  we.keycards(N)>=3
  4N  "Sign off: two aces missing"
      when  we.keycards(N).max<=2
  6N  "Small slam: \"0 or 4\" with no aces of my own is 4"
      when  maybe we.keycards(N)>=3
      priority -1

when asked gerber_kings
  5D  "0 or 4 kings"  shows (controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) = 0) | (controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) = 4)   artificial
  5H  "1 king"        shows controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) = 1   artificial
  5S  "2 kings"       shows controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) = 2   artificial
  5N  "3 kings"       shows controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) = 3   artificial

# All four aces are ours (the king ask needs them): seven with all four
# kings as well, else six. Kings are controls less two for each ace.
when answered gerber_kings
  7N  "Grand slam: all the aces and kings"
      when  (partner.last=5N, controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) >= 1) | (partner.last=5S, controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) >= 2) | (partner.last=5H, controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) >= 3) | (partner.last=5D, controls - keycards(N) - keycards(N) >= 4)
      priority 1
  6N  "Small slam: a king missing"
